%% # Scene 06 — analyzer error during sampling, needle left down (turnstile)
%% # Same situation as scene 05, with the turnstile, gate and antenna of scene 02.
%% # The wheel can't rotate while the needle is down: after the recovery and
%% # Status (Ready) it brings the carrier to the exit and releases it.
%% # Carrier flow: right to left, Pit-Lane above the Main-Lane.
%% # Coordinates are in a fixed 1920x1080 space (track panel: x 30..950, y 120..885).
%% # Points left of x=30 or right of x=950 are outside the panel (hidden).
%% geometry turnstile
%% subtitle Single carrier — analyzer error with the needle down, operator recovery (turnstile)
sequenceDiagram
    participant IF as Interface
    participant AN as Analyzer
    participant DMX as DMX

    %% carrier id=C1 sid=SID-000123 route=main_in,pit_entry,pit_exit,gone

    %% caption 1 · Turnstile with gate and antenna | A carrier holding a sample tube travels towards the interface. The Pit-Lane ends in a turnstile, with an antenna and a gate in front of it.
    %% at 2.6
    %% move C1 to pit_wait
    %% on antenna1 C1
    %% caption 2 · Diverted — Prepare — antenna | The carrier is diverted without stopping (Prepare) and read at the antenna (Prepare again). Nothing is being sampled, so the gate opens, the carrier enters and the wheel brings it under the needle.
    %% on antenna1
    IF->>AN: Prepare SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    AN-->>IF: OK SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.5 antenna2 C1
    %% color #9333EA
    IF->>AN: Prepare SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    AN->>DMX: Query SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 Prepare C1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
    %% after 0.1 Query C1
    DMX-->>AN: Tests to perform SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    %% pass antenna2
    %% after 0.15
    %% rotate ts
    %% after 0.25
    %% caption 3 · Sample Acquisition | The carrier is under the needle: the interface sends Sample Acquisition and the analyzer starts aspirating.
    %% after 0.25 rotate ts
    IF->>AN: Sample Acquisition SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
    %% after 0.1
    %% needle ts down
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    %% duration 2.6
    Note over AN: Pipetting Analyzer - SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 1.7 needle ts
    %% caption 4 · Instrument error | During aspiration the analyzer goes into error, leaving the needle down in the tube. It immediately sends its status (Error) and Sample Complete. The interface replies OK to the status.
    %% after 1.7 needle ts
    %% status analyzer error
    %% after 1.7 needle ts
    %% for C1
    AN->>IF: Status State=Error
    AN->>IF: Sample Complete SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.3 Status C1
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 0.1 Sample Complete C1
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% caption 5 · Operator recovery | Sample Complete is not enough: with the analyzer in error the wheel does not rotate, the needle is still in the tube. An operator comes to the instrument for a recovery: the needle goes back up.
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% duration 6
    Note over AN: Operator recovery
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% operator analyzer duration=7
    %% after 4.6 Status C1
    %% needle ts up duration=1.2
    %% after 2.6
    %% caption 6 · Instrument ready | The instrument is green again: it sends its status (Ready) to the interface, which replies OK. Only now the carrier is released.
    %% after 2.6 needle ts
    %% status analyzer ready
    %% after 2.6 needle ts
    %% for C1
    AN->>IF: Status State=Ready
    %% after 0.2
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 1.5 Status C1
    %% status analyzer normal
    %% after 0.2 OK C1
    %% caption 7 · Carrier released — Release | The wheel brings the carrier to the exit and the interface releases it. As soon as it has left the interface module, the interface sends Release.
    %% after 1.9 Status C1
    %% rotate ts
    %% after 0.2
    %% move C1 to gone
    %% on antenna3
    IF->>AN: Release SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
